## Summary
Italian prosecutors allege that COVID-19 data was manipulated by officials in Liguria, with Governor Giovanni Toti reportedly admitting to inflating infection numbers. Toti allegedly told his chief of staff Matteo Cozzani that he had slightly increased the reported case figures.

## Key Points
- Prosecutors allege systematic manipulation of COVID-19 statistics in Liguria
- Governor Giovanni Toti is accused of admitting to increasing infection numbers
- Toti reportedly discussed the alterations with his chief of staff Matteo Cozzani
- The allegations center on the handling of pandemic data rather than clinical outcomes


